; Self test of the port-only fixed form of the TED bug-orig tests
; (tests/bug-orig/CMakeLists.txt): "; @fixed-orig #N Cc".  The expectation does
; not hold of TED-C (the output of the command ends with rc=0, not rc=7), as
; if the fixed bug came back: the Cc run must be REGRESSED (exit status 1,
; naming the bug).  The C5 run behaves the same, as the recorded original
; says: REPRODUCED (1), the bug that the original compiler keeps.  99999 is
; no issue.
; @fixed-orig #99999 Cc
; @source none
; @expect stdout "rc=7"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
